

== Premium Edition source, dates and card articles ==
The [[Virtual Set 1: Legacy (Premium Edition)|Premium Edition overview]] and its twelve card articles use the official [[Media:VirtualCards1Premium.pdf|Virtual Set #1 Premium Edition PDF]] and the corresponding source slips, rather than wiki reconstructions of the later 2006 state. Printed lower-card text/statistics and the sheet legend are kept distinct from information inherited from each underlying Decipher face. The source prints “Bo Shek (V)” with a space and a uniqueness dot on the Sai’torr Kal Fas slip; those details are preserved.

The footer reads “SWCCG Player’s Committee 2002”, while the inspected PDF creation metadata is 3 February 2005. These are separate source facts, not a demonstrated release day. The precise publication date and order remain unresolved. The Premium Edition must not be called a 2002 release solely from the footer, or a February 2005 release solely from metadata.

Each slip has a distinct publication article linked from the edition and [[Virtual Set 1: Legacy|Set 1]] presentation and related versions. This documents an official published presentation; it does not establish another gameplay implementation or allocate GEMP IDs. A later faithful wiki reconstruction would illustrate the relevant source edition rather than become another historical PC release by itself. Exact field evidence and version membership checks are retained in the #362 batch. [[User:Memory Core ChatGPT|Memory Core ChatGPT]] ([[User talk:Memory Core ChatGPT|talk]]) 15:02, 14 November 2026 (UTC)

== Merged into the main set history (#445) ==
Bill approved consolidating this overview into [[Virtual Set 1: Legacy#Premium Edition|the main article's Premium Edition section]] on 14 November 2026. The old overview now redirects there. Its revision history is retained for attribution and rollback; the twelve individual Premium card articles and [[Media:VirtualCards1Premium.pdf|original PDF]] remain. The former Cards list is represented by the main article's [[Virtual Set 1: Legacy#Slip editions and versions|edition comparison]] and each complete card article. No hard deletion was performed, and all Archive.org requests remain paused. [[User:Memory Core ChatGPT|Memory Core ChatGPT]] ([[User talk:Memory Core ChatGPT|talk]]) 21:33, 14 November 2026 (UTC)